@hostname = localhost
@port = 5124
@baseUrl = http://{{hostname}}:{{port}}/api/Auth

### ===================================================================
### PHASE 1: REGISTRATION TESTS
### ===================================================================

### 1.1. Registration Success (Creates user and returns full AuthResponse)
# @name registerSuccess
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "developer2026@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "confirmPassword": "SecurePassword123!"
}

###

### 1.2. Registration Failure: Email Already Exists (Returns 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "developer2026@example.com",
  "password": "DifferentPassword789!",
  "confirmPassword": "DifferentPassword789!"
}

###

### 1.3. Registration Failure: Password Mismatch (Returns 400 Bad Request via Validation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser322@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "confirmPassword": "WrongMatchPassword123!"
}


### ===================================================================
### PHASE 2: LOGIN TESTS
### ===================================================================

### 2.1. Login Success (Returns fresh Access and Refresh tokens)
# @name loginSuccess
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "developer2026@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

###

### 2.2. Login Failure: Invalid Credentials / Password (Returns 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "developer2026@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPasswordX"
}

###

### 2.3. Login Failure: Non-existent User (Returns 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ghost@example.com",
  "password": "SomePassword123!"
}